Recognise uclinux* as a host that can build shared libraries

ncurses' configure decides whether shared libraries are possible from a case on
the host triple. Our toolchain is arm-buildroot-uclinuxfdpiceabi, so $host_os is
"uclinuxfdpiceabi", which matches neither `linux*` nor `gnu*` and falls through
to the (*) branch:

	(*)
		CC_SHARED_OPTS='unknown'
		MK_SHARED_LIB='echo unknown'

after which configure stops with "Shared libraries are not supported in this
version" -- on a toolchain it had probed three lines earlier and which answered
-fPIC. uClibc FDPIC builds shared libraries perfectly well; the whole userspace
depends on a shared libc.so, and on an 8 MB NOMMU system that sharing is what
makes running more than one program possible at all.

Other parts of this same configure already list uclinux* alongside the linux
variants, so these two cases are an omission rather than a policy.

Signed-off-by: Mikhail Matveev <xtreme@rh1.tech>

--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -6792,7 +6792,7 @@
 			LD_RPATH_OPT="-rpath "
 		fi
 		;;
-	(linux*|gnu*|k*bsd*-gnu|freebsd*)
+	(linux*|uclinux*|gnu*|k*bsd*-gnu|freebsd*)
 		LD_RPATH_OPT="-Wl,-rpath,"
 		;;
 	(openbsd[2-9].*|mirbsd*)
@@ -7151,7 +7151,7 @@
 		fi
 		cf_cv_rm_so_locs=yes
 		;;
-	(linux*|gnu*|k*bsd*-gnu)
+	(linux*|uclinux*|gnu*|k*bsd*-gnu)
 		if test "$DFT_LWR_MODEL" = "shared" && test -n "$LD_RPATH_OPT" ; then
 			LOCAL_LDFLAGS="${LD_RPATH_OPT}\$(LOCAL_LIBDIR)"
 			LOCAL_LDFLAGS2="$LOCAL_LDFLAGS"
